 in the Southern vs. the Northern hemisphere</article-title><source>Psychiatry Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>112</volume><fpage>89</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12379455</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0165-1781(02)00183-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mino</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Oshima</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Okagami</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Seasonality of birth in patients with mood disorders in Japan</article-title><source>J Affect Disord</source><year>2000</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>41</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10814769</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0165-0327(99)00130-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Crow</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Done</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prenatal exposure to influenza does not cause schizophrenia</article-title><source>Br J Psychiatry</source><year>1992</year><volume>161</volume><fpage>390</fpage><lpage>393</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1393309</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Takei</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Callaghan</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Sham</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>Glover</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Does prenatal influenza divert susceptible females from later affective psychosis to schizophrenia?</article-title><source>Acta Psychiatr Scand</source